Description: 3MF thumbnails: the slicer's picture first, F3D's stereo pair when there is none, and the person's option (ORDER 17)
 KIO took model/3mf for the compiled opendocumentthumbnail plugin, which reads only a thumbnail embedded in the file, so a 3MF
 without one got no picture although F3D's thumbnailer (a standard thumbnailer, which a compiled plugin shadows) draws it.
 A plugin of its own, threemfthumbnail, takes the type: the picture the slicer embedded (Metadata/thumbnail.png) first, then
 the model drawn as a stereo pair by f3d-thumbnail-pair (the F3D of Sparky Stereo OS), and the other way round when the person
 sets ThreeMFPreferRender=true in the PreviewSettings group of kdeglobals.
